2. Executive Summary

ASE is a research‑grade computational instrument that integrates astrophysical datasets with microphysical proton–laser interaction physics. It merges cosmic‑ray spectra, ISM density maps, star‑formation models, and GEANT4 particle datasets with PIC, Vlasov–Maxwell, and MHD solvers inside a GPU‑accelerated, zero‑trust‑secured HPC framework.

ASE enables proton‑laser simulations under astrophysical boundary conditions — a capability not present in existing scientific tools. This submission package provides the documentation required for institutional review, validation, and adoption.

